~ arrive
Traveller: So this is the other side of it.
Traveller: Nobody's been through in years, he said. Somebody's kept a lamp lit.
=> END

~ lantern
Somebody's lantern, left burning by the path. The oil is nearly gone and it has been trimmed recently.
=> END

~ rope
A coil of rope, old but sound, tied off to a stake driven into the rock. Whoever left it meant to come back down.
=> END

~ ledge
The path has gone to sand here, and past the sand the ground drops away to the sea.
Some of it will take your weight. It does not say which.
=> END

~ rest
Traveller: [[A fire's a fire. I'll take the log.|The old man won't mind. He said as much.|Just till it's light.]]
=> END

~ rest_woke
Traveller: [[Cold. Grey. Morning, then.|The fire's down to embers. Up.|Slept. Didn't dream, which is something.]]
=> END
